<BlogPostLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  category="career-options"
  publishedAt={publishedDateISO}
  publishedLabel={publishedDateLabel}
  authorName={authorName}
  authorUrl={authorUrl}
  authorRole={authorRole}
  jsonLdExtras={[faqJsonLd]}
>
  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>Career options after NEET depend on three numbers you can look up today: your rank in your own category, the quota you fall under, and what the seat costs against what it can earn.</strong>
    A government MBBS seat is the best value on the list. Everything below it needs a fee test, and a backup lane keeps one bad round from costing a year.
  </p>

  <p class="lead-para">
    The decisions you make now unlock high income opportunities later. A skill portfolio built beside the degree moves you toward earlier financial freedom.
  </p>

  <div class="key-takeaways">
    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li>In 2026 about 20 lakh students sat NEET and 11.21 lakh qualified, for 1,40,664 MBBS seats on the latest NMC matrix. That is about 8 qualifiers for every MBBS seat and about 17.5 for every government seat.</li>
      <li>Qualifying is not a seat. Your category closing rank decides: in Round 2 the general line closed near rank 25,655 and the SC line near 1,20,870.</li>
      <li>Private seats are a money decision. One college lists Rs 95.83 lakh for a management seat against about Rs 2.6 lakh at a government college. Avoid education debt unless the licence needs it.</li>
      <li><strong>Next step: find your category closing rank, list every seat with its full fee, and keep a backup lane and one skill running beside the main plan.</strong></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p>
    If you want a person to test your shortlist against your rank, budget and family situation, our <a href="/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/career-counselling-for-neet-aspirants/">career counselling for NEET aspirants</a> is built for this decision. For a wider view of every route, see <a href="/blog/career-options/">our career options guides</a>.
  </p>

  <nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="Article sections">
    <p class="jump-nav__label">Jump to section</p>
    <ul class="jump-nav__list">
      {jumpLinks.map((item) => (
        <li><a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.label}</a></li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <h2 id="answer">The direct answer: read your category line, then the fee, then the lane</h2>

  <p>
    Most pages list courses. The harder part comes after the result: which seat your rank can reach, how counselling really works, and whether the fee is safe.
  </p>

  <p>
    This guide is for a student who already holds a NEET (UG) score. If you did not sit the exam or chose not to, start with <a href="/blog/career-options/pcb-career-options-without-neet/">PCB career options without NEET</a>.
  </p>

