  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>The ownership path:</strong> a clinic with associates, a diagnostic centre, a health-tech product, medical writing and clinical consulting all let you set price and reach beyond your own hours, because you can hire, repeat work or serve people remotely. Each needs a licence, capital or a proof shelf, and years of trust.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    A medical, dental or AYUSH licence needs the formal degree, supervised training and registration. No video course replaces that. What you can learn cheaply beside it is the skill layer: patient communication in English and your local language, clinical writing, spreadsheets and data basics, and safe use of AI. Good YouTube channels, official guidelines and reputable low-cost courses cover much of this, but a certificate is not proof. A finished patient-education asset, a small audit or a case summary is.
  </p>

  <p>
    This is the high-value skill portfolio idea in practice: one core skill (your clinical training), one multiplier skill (communication, data or writing) and visible proof. It is how the decisions you make now unlock high income opportunities, whichever seat you take.
  </p>

  <h2 id="runway">Two stages of competition: the seat, then the specialist seat</h2>

  <p>
    The minimum to practise medicine is the MBBS (4.5 years), a compulsory rotating internship of at least twelve months, then permanent registration. A postgraduate degree is not a legal requirement for every doctor. For a specialist career it is a practical one, and it is a second competition.
  </p>

