  <h2 id="drop">The drop-year decision, with your category numbers</h2>

  <p>
    A drop year is a bet on one stage. Use three numbers before you pay for it.
  </p>

  <ol class="rich-list">
    <li><strong>The gap.</strong> Take the Round 2 closing rank for your category and the seat you would accept, from the table above. Compare it with an honest mock rank, not your best day.</li>
    <li><strong>The full cost.</strong> Coaching, living cost and a year of delayed pay, plus doors that close. The BPT and BOT window on Class 12 marks may end after this cycle, and some doors have age limits.</li>
    <li><strong>The evidence.</strong> NTA reports that over 93% of the 138 candidates above 690 marks sat NEET for the first time. NTA gives no repeater success rate and no verified dataset turned up, so claims of large gains come from coaching sites.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
